# D-Card API — guest card page (public, no login)
# The link token is the credential. Responses are `no-store`; the page is `noindex` and sends no Referer.
# Contribution amounts are never returned here (CON-12).


### Setup: event with an issued card
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hostToken}}

###
# @name event
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/events
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hostToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "planKey": "kawaida", "eventTypeKey": "wedding", "title": "Harusi ya Juma na Neema", "startsAt": "2026-12-12T15:00:00+03:00", "venueName": "Diamond Jubilee Hall", "venueAddress": "Upanga, Dar es Salaam", "contactName": "Asha", "contactPhone": "0754123456" }

> {%
  client.global.set("eventId", response.body.id);
%}

###
# @name guest
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/events/{{eventId}}/guests
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hostToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Juma Salum", "phone": "0713700001", "cardType": "double", "partnerName": "Neema", "consent": true }

> {%
  client.global.set("guestId", response.body.guest.id);
%}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/events/{{eventId}}/guests/{{guestId}}/issue
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hostToken}}

### Get the card link; its token is saved for the public requests below
# The page itself is <baseUrl>/c/<token> (open the returned link in a browser).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/events/{{eventId}}/guests/{{guestId}}/card
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hostToken}}

> {%
  client.global.set("cardToken", response.body.link.split("/c/")[1]);
%}

### Card by link token (public)
# 200 → { status: issued|cancelled, guestName, partnerName, cardType, cardNumber, qrToken (null when cancelled),
#   rsvp: { status: none|yes|no, dietaryNotes, at, open }, event: { title, typeKey, typeNameSw, typeNameEn, startsAt, endsAt,
#   timeZone, venueName, venueAddress, venueMapUrl, contactName, contactPhone, status } }
# 404 unknown or malformed token.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cards/{{cardToken}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### RSVP Yes/No with a dietary note (public; editable until the event starts)
# Body: answer yes|no, dietaryNotes? (≤ 300 chars).
# 200 → { status, dietaryNotes, at, open } · 409 card cancelled or event started · 422 other answers · 429 more than 20 writes per card per hour.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cards/{{cardToken}}/rsvp
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "answer": "yes", "dietaryNotes": "Sili nyama ya nguruwe" }

### "maybe" is not an option → 422
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cards/{{cardToken}}/rsvp
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "answer": "maybe" }

### Add to calendar (.ics, text/calendar)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cards/{{cardToken}}/calendar.ics
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Card image with QR (PNG 1080×1350, rendered on demand, not stored)
# lang sw (default) or en. 404 for cancelled or unknown cards. Used for download now and WhatsApp in phase 03.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cards/{{cardToken}}/image?lang={{locale}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Unknown token → 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cards/AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
